{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/cavaliers-of-mars-and-pugmire/1188538-pugmire-what-s-the-size-of-the-typical-rat","id":1188538,"title":"Pugmire: What's the size of the typical rat?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Partner Worlds","Realms of Pugmire"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-22T09:23:30-08:00","id":1188538,"title":"Pugmire: What's the size of the typical rat?","content":"In the chapter describing enemies there are Road Rat stats, that claim rat's size to be Tiny (Speed 10; 4 base stamina points per CR); and Labo Tor cultists' stats that are of Medium Size (Speed 30; 8 base stamina points per CR). So, where is a mistake here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6186-aleksay","name":"Aleksay","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T12:39:25-08:00","id":1190390,"title":"","content":"Not a mistake -- not all of the mechanics map directly to size (which is why size was removed from all enemies). You can (and probably should) adjust mechanics, but size offers a handy starting point for making your own enemies. If you absolutely need to map them to 5e size, rats are Medium, regardless of mechanics. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15-eddyfate","name":"eddyfate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thank